{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "LevelSetReinitWRFFire",
  "description": "The level-set REINITIALISATION equation of NCAR fire_behavior (physics/level_set_mod.F90 Reinit_level_set / Advance_ls_reinit; Sussman, Smereka and Osher 1994 as adapted by Munoz-Esparza et al. 2018), written as the PDE d psi / d tau = S(psi_0) (1 - |grad psi|) on cartesian_uniform_2d and lowered by the EarthSciDiscretizations rule each test imports. WHAT THIS IS AND IS NOT. It is NOT part of d psi/dt: the fire model propagates the level set, then re-signs it in a pseudo-time loop between the propagation and the ignition-time update, so the instantaneous tendency that couplings/wildlandfire_behavior.esm exposes is untouched by anything here. What it is, is the operator that keeps psi close to a signed distance function, which matters for two reasons: the WENO5/ENO1 band test of the PROPAGATION scheme is written on |psi| itself, so a psi that drifts away from a distance function silently changes which discretisation each cell gets; and a long .esm integration that omits it will diverge from WRF's for that reason even though every instantaneous tendency agrees. ACCEPTANCE: this component's own pseudo-time tendency is verified against the Fortran; it makes no claim about d psi/dt. THE SIGN IS FROZEN. S(psi_0) = psi_0 / sqrt(psi_0^2 + dx^2) is formed ONCE per reinitialisation from the field the propagation left (fire_behavior's lfn_s0, from lfn_out) and reused by all three Runge-Kutta stages, so psi_ref is a separate input from psi and is NOT psi at stages 2 and 3. The stage-2 test is what proves the component keeps it frozen. It is also the upwind selector: the hybrid WENO5/ENO1 derivative picks its side from S(psi_0) (d4 psi/dx), not from the wind-relative sign the propagation uses, which is why this component imports the rule weno5_eno1_signed_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc and supplies the free name upwind_sign rather than wind_u/wind_v. UNITS, stated because they are odd and the oddity is the reference code's: the reinitialisation's pseudo-time step is dt_s = reinit_pseudot_coef * dx, which is a LENGTH, and the tendency S (1 - |grad psi|) is DIMENSIONLESS, so the update lfn_fin = lfn_ini + dt_s * rk_coeff * tend_r is metres + metres and is consistent -- but the quantity fire_behavior calls a time step is a length and what it calls a tendency has no units. tau_step and dpsi_dtau are declared accordingly rather than being given a fictitious second. HOW MUCH IT MOVES psi, measured rather than assumed: at the coefficient both shipped namelists set (reinit_pseudot_coef = 0.0001, against the namelist_mod default of 0.01) one reinitialisation of one WRF step changes psi by at most 5.7 mm and on average 0.14 mm, i.e. 2.3e-4 of the 25 m cell, while rms(|grad psi| - 1) over the domain is 0.177. So on test7 the reinitialisation is very nearly inert, and the 100x larger namelist default -- what a user who does not copy test7's namelist gets -- would make it 0.57 m per step, 2.3 % of a cell. Not transcribed: Reinit_level_set's outer loop (fire_lsm_reinit_iter Runge-Kutta iterations, default 1), its final `lfn_out = min(lfn_s3, lfn_in)` clamp (\"fire area can only increase\"), and Reinit_level_set_fast_dist (the fast-sweeping option, fast_dist_reinit_opt). Reference: fire_behavior develop @ eb77580, instrumented fork ctessum-claude/fire_behavior@66a800e, real32, rel 1e-5. TOLERANCE ON dpsi_dtau, measured not guessed: the tendency is S (1 - |grad psi|), and near the front |grad psi| is within a few 1e-3 of 1, so the subtraction loses about 2.5 decimal digits to cancellation out of real32's 7. The floor is therefore an ABSOLUTE 2e-7 alongside the relative 2e-5, which is roughly three ulps of the dumped grad_mag: at (18,64), 1 - grad = 3.879e-3 with eps32(grad) = 5.96e-8, giving |S| eps32 = 1.9e-8 against an observed residual of 3.2e-8, and at (20,66) 4.2e-8 against 7.0e-8 -- a couple of ulps in both cases, i.e. the reference's own precision and not a transcription difference. Where there is no cancellation the relative tolerance still governs: at (17,57) the tendency is -1.71 and 2e-7 is 1.2e-7 relative, far tighter than 2e-5, so the floor never makes an assertion vacuous.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wildland_fire",
   "fire_behavior",
   "level-set",
   "reinitialisation",
   "pde"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580, physics/level_set_mod.F90: Reinit_level_set, Advance_ls_reinit. Instrumented fork ctessum-claude/fire_behavior branch earthsciml-instrumented @ 66a800e (the ls_reinit dump hook)."
   },
   {
    "citation": "Sussman, M., P. Smereka and S. Osher (1994), A level set approach for computing solutions to incompressible two-phase flow, Journal of Computational Physics 114, 146-159.",
    "doi": "10.1006/jcph.1994.1155"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Munoz-Esparza, D., B. Kosovic, P. A. Jimenez and J. L. Coen (2018), An accurate fire-spread algorithm in the Weather Research and Forecasting model using the level-set method, JAMES 10, 908-926.",
    "doi": "10.1002/2017MS001108"
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NX": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 80,
   "description": "Fire-mesh cells in x (test7 ifde - ifds + 1 = 80)."
  },
  "NY": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 80,
   "description": "Fire-mesh cells in y."
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "LevelSetReinitWRFFire": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/grid.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NX": "NX",
      "NY": "NY"
     }
    }
   ],
   "variables": {
    "x0": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "West edge of the fire mesh (grid geometry contract)."
    },
    "y0": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "South edge of the fire mesh."
    },
    "Lx": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 2000.0,
     "description": "Fire-mesh extent in x (test7: 80 cells of 25 m)."
    },
    "Ly": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 2000.0,
     "description": "Fire-mesh extent in y."
    },
    "dx": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "Cell size in x, Lx/NX; also the smoothing length of the sign function."
    },
    "dy": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "Cell size in y, Ly/NY."
    },
    "bdy_eno1_cells": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 10,
     "description": "Cells from a wall within which the derivative drops to ENO1 (fire_behavior BDY_ENO1 = 10). Free name required by the imported rule."
    },
    "weno_band_cells": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 4,
     "description": "Band half-width in cells within which WENO5 is used (fire_lsm_band_ngp = 4; threshold_hlu = weno_band_cells dx). Free name required by the imported rule. NOTE the reinitialisation's band test is SIGNED, psi >= weno_band_cells dx selects ENO1, not |psi| >= ... -- see the rule's description and FORTRAN_BUGS."
    },
    "reinit_pseudot_coef": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.0001,
     "description": "Coefficient of the pseudo-time step, dt_s = reinit_pseudot_coef dx. Both shipped namelists set 1e-4; namelist_mod's default is 1e-2."
    },
    "psi": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "The level set at this Runge-Kutta stage of the reinitialisation (fire_behavior lfn_curr), consumer-supplied through `input_psi`. The component does not own it: the consumer drives the pseudo-time iteration."
    },
    "psi_ref": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "The level set the smoothed sign is FROZEN from, i.e. the field the propagation left before the reinitialisation started (fire_behavior lfn_out, the source of lfn_s0). Equal to psi at stage 1 only. Consumer-supplied through `input_psi_ref`."
    },
    "upwind_sign": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "The smoothed sign S(psi_0) = psi_ref / sqrt(psi_ref^2 + dx^2) (fire_behavior lfn_s0). It is both the coefficient of the reinitialisation forcing and the free name by which the imported rule chooses each cell's upwind side."
    },
    "grad_mag": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "|grad psi| from the signed-upwind hybrid WENO5/ENO1 derivative (fire_behavior grad_norm_reinit). Dimensionless: metres of psi per metre of distance."
    },
    "dpsi_dtau": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "x",
      "y"
     ],
     "description": "TENDENCY: the pseudo-time right-hand side S(psi_0) (1 - |grad psi|) (fire_behavior tend_r). Dimensionless because the pseudo-time variable is a length -- see the component description."
    },
    "tau_step": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "The pseudo-time step fire_behavior takes, dt_s = reinit_pseudot_coef dx. A length, not a time."
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "dx",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       "Lx",
       "NX"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "dy",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       "Ly",
       "NY"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "psi",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "input_psi",
      "args": []
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "psi_ref",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "input_psi_ref",
      "args": []
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "upwind_sign",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       "psi_ref",
       {
        "op": "sqrt",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "+",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "^",
            "args": [
             "psi_ref",
             2
            ]
           },
           {
            "op": "^",
            "args": [
             "dx",
             2
            ]
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "grad_mag",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "sqrt",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
             "psi"
            ],
            "wrt": "x"
           },
           2
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
             "psi"
            ],
            "wrt": "y"
           },
           2
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "dpsi_dtau",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "upwind_sign",
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         1.0,
         "grad_mag"
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "tau_step",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "reinit_pseudot_coef",
       "dx"
      ]
     }
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "reinit_step20_stage1",
     "description": "Runge-Kutta stage 1 of the reinitialisation of step 20 (ts = 10 s) of the fire_behavior test7 standalone run with fire_upwinding_reinit = 4 (the default hybrid WENO5/ENO1), fire_lsm_band_ngp = 4, BDY_ENO1 = 10, reinit_pseudot_coef = 1e-4 on a 25 m mesh. At this stage psi_ref = psi, because lfn_s0 is formed from lfn_out and stage 1 is handed lfn_out unchanged -- the identity S = psi/sqrt(psi^2+dx^2) was checked against the dumped lfn_s0 to 1.0e-7. Reference: data/eqwefic/dumps/fire/run_reinit/esm_dump_ls_reinit_58.json, real32, rel 2e-5 (the WENO5 smoothness weights amplify single-precision rounding, the same tolerance the propagation component's hybrid tests use). Cells span the regimes: (18,64) and (20,66) inside the band at the front where the sign is small; (17,57) just outside the front with |grad psi| = 2.89, the largest departure from a distance function in the domain; (40,40), (50,30), (70,70) and (12,12) in the far field on the ENO1 branch; (5,40) inside the ENO1 wall strip.",
     "expression_template_imports": [
      {
       "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/weno5_eno1_signed_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc.esm",
       "bindings": {
        "NX": 80,
        "NY": 80
       }
      },
      {
       "ref": "./tests/reinit_step20_stage1_inputs.esm"
      }
     ],
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "Lx": 2000.0,
      "Ly": 2000.0,
      "bdy_eno1_cells": 10,
      "weno_band_cells": 4,
      "reinit_pseudot_coef": 0.0001
     },
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 1
     },
     "tolerance": {
      "rel": 2e-05
     },
     "assertions": [
      {
       "variable": "tau_step",
       "time": 0.0,
       "expected": 0.0025,
       "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-05
       }
      },
      {
       "variable": "upwind_sign",
       "time": 0.0,
       "coords": {
        "x": 18,
        "y": 64
       },
       "expected": -0.31077396869659424,
