    {
     "id": "reinit_step20_stage2",
     "description": "Runge-Kutta stage 2 of the same reinitialisation (dump esm_dump_ls_reinit_59.json). psi has advanced to the stage-1 output lfn_s1 while psi_ref is still the pre-reinitialisation lfn_out, because fire_behavior freezes lfn_s0 once per reinitialisation -- the dumped lfn_s0 is bit-identical between calls 58 and 59. MEASURED, because the obvious claim is false: this test does NOT discriminate a frozen sign from a recomputed one. At the shipped reinit_pseudot_coef = 1e-4 the field moves only 1.9 mm between stages, so recomputing S from the current psi changes it by at most 5.6e-5 relative anywhere in the domain (1.1e-7 to 4.7e-6 at the cells asserted here) -- below the 2e-5 tolerance. Substituting psi_ref := psi in this test leaves all 29 assertions passing. The test that does discriminate is reinit_default_coef_step20_stage2; this one is kept because it is the shipped regime. Same tolerances and cells as stage 1.",
