    {
     "id": "reinit_default_coef_step20_stage2",
     "description": "THE TEST THAT PROVES THE SIGN IS FROZEN. Same Runge-Kutta stage 2 of the same step, but from a rerun of test7 at reinit_pseudot_coef = 0.01 -- namelist_mod's default, which is 100x what both shipped namelists set. The larger pseudo-time step (dt_s = 0.25 m against 0.0025 m) moves psi 0.19 m between stages instead of 1.9 mm, and that is what makes the frozen sign observable: recomputing S(psi_0) from the CURRENT field instead of from the pre-reinitialisation one would change upwind_sign by 5.6e-3 relative at cell (21,59), 281x this test's 2e-5 tolerance, and dpsi_dtau there by the same amount with no cancellation to hide it (|tend| = 1.38). Verified by substitution: replacing psi_ref with psi in this test's input library fails it. Cell (21,59) is the domain maximum of that sensitivity among cells with |tend| > 0.05; (17,57) is the next largest at 4.7e-4. The far-field cells are insensitive (7.5e-9 and below) because S saturates at +-1 away from the front, which is itself the reason the shipped-coefficient test cannot discriminate. Reference: data/eqwefic/dumps/fire/run_reinit2/esm_dump_ls_reinit_{58,59}.json, real32.",
